      {"q":"What is double 35?","o":["55","70","65","75"],"a":1,"e":"Double means add the number to itself: 35 + 35 = 70."},
      {"q":"What is half of 48?","o":["12","22","24","26"],"a":2,"e":"Half of 40 is 20 and half of 8 is 4, so half of 48 is 24."},
      {"q":"What is a quarter of 40?","o":["8","20","10","4"],"a":2,"e":"A quarter means one of four equal parts: 40 ÷ 4 = 10."},
      {"q":"How many sides does an octagon have?","o":["6","7","10","8"],"a":3,"e":"Octa means eight, so an octagon has eight straight sides, like a stop sign. 🛑"},
      {"q":"How many flat faces does a cube have?","o":["4","6","8","12"],"a":1,"e":"A cube has a top, a bottom and four sides, which makes six flat faces."},
      {"q":"The clock shows 3:45. How many minutes are left until 4 o'clock?","o":["15 minutes","45 minutes","10 minutes","20 minutes"],"a":0,"e":"From 45 minutes to 60 minutes is 15 minutes, so 4 o'clock is a quarter of an hour away. ⏰"},
      {"q":"A movie starts at 6:30 and lasts 90 minutes. What time does it end?","o":["7:20","7:30","8:30","8:00"],"a":3,"e":"90 minutes is one hour and 30 minutes: 6:30 plus one hour is 7:30, plus 30 minutes is 8:00. 🎬"},
      {"q":"What time is quarter past seven in the morning?","o":["7:45","7:15","6:45","7:30"],"a":1,"e":"A quarter of an hour is 15 minutes, so quarter past seven is 7:15."},
      {"q":"In mathematics, what do we call the answer you get when you add numbers together?","o":["The product","The sum","The difference","The quotient"],"a":1,"e":"Each operation has its own word for the answer: add gives a sum, multiply gives a product, subtract gives a difference and divide gives a quotient."},
      {"q":"What is 100 - 37?","o":["67","73","63","57"],"a":2,"e":"A quick way to check a subtraction is to add it back: 63 plus 37 gives 100."},
      {"q":"How many minutes are in a quarter of an hour?","o":["30","20","10","15"],"a":3,"e":"A quarter means one part out of four, and 60 minutes divided by 4 gives 15. That is why we say quarter past and quarter to."},
      {"q":"Which shape has three equal sides and three equal angles?","o":["A square","An equilateral triangle","A rectangle","A pentagon"],"a":1,"e":"The word equilateral comes from Latin and means equal sides. Each of its three angles measures 60 degrees."},
      {"q":"You buy a snack for 3.75 dollars and pay with a 5 dollar bill. How much change do you get?","o":["1.25 dollars","2.25 dollars","1.35 dollars","1.75 dollars"],"a":0,"e":"Counting up is easier than subtracting: from 3.75 to 4.00 is 25 cents, then 4.00 to 5.00 is one dollar."},
      {"q":"What is 0.5 written as a fraction?","o":["1/5","1/4","1/2","5/1"],"a":2,"e":"The first place after the decimal point counts tenths, so 0.5 is 5 tenths, and 5/10 simplifies to 1/2."},
      {"q":"What number comes next: 5, 10, 15, 20?","o":["22","24","30","25"],"a":3,"e":"Each step adds 5, so this is simply the five times table. Counting by fives is a handy skill for reading clocks."},
      {"q":"How many degrees are in a right angle?","o":["45 degrees","90 degrees","180 degrees","60 degrees"],"a":1,"e":"A right angle is the square corner you see on a book or a door frame. Four of them together make a full turn of 360 degrees."},
      {"q":"How many Canadian quarters (25-cent coins) make one dollar?","o":["4","5","10","2"],"a":0,"e":"A quarter is worth one quarter of a dollar, and 25 times 4 equals 100 cents."},
      {"q":"What is 7 multiplied by 8?","o":["56","54","63","48"],"a":0,"e":"Seven eights are fifty-six."},
      {"q":"What is 12 divided by 4?","o":["2","3","4","6"],"a":1,"e":"Twelve divided by four is three."},
      {"q":"What is half of one hundred?","o":["25","40","50","75"],"a":2,"e":"Half of one hundred is fifty."},
      {"q":"How many minutes are there in one hour?","o":["60","30","100","24"],"a":0,"e":"There are sixty minutes in an hour and sixty seconds in a minute."},
      {"q":"Which number comes next: 2, 4, 6, 8, …?","o":["9","10","11","12"],"a":1,"e":"The numbers go up by two each time, so ten comes next."},
      {"q":"What is double 25?","o":["45","40","50","55"],"a":2,"e":"Double twenty-five is fifty."},
      {"q":"What is 100 minus 45?","o":["55","65","45","35"],"a":0,"e":"One hundred take away forty-five leaves fifty-five."},
      {"q":"What shape has four equal sides and four right angles?","o":["A rectangle","A square","A rhombus","A trapezoid"],"a":1,"e":"A square has four equal sides and four right angles. A rectangle has right angles but its sides need not all match."},
      {"q":"How many months have exactly 31 days?","o":["Five","Six","Seven","Eight"],"a":2,"e":"January, March, May, July, August, October and December — seven months."},
      {"q":"What is a quarter of 20?","o":["5","4","10","6"],"a":0,"e":"A quarter means divided by four, and twenty divided by four is five."}
